      "message": "feat(sim): the scallop flank reads to the ball diameter, between contact passes only\n\nThe ridge flank judged a column only within band + 3·tol of two passes,\nso on flat ground a cusp was read only to 4·tol past the ball (s ~ 2.9\non an r3 ball at tol 0.1); a wider spacing verified silent. #37 measured\na plain 2r window convicting 11 finish3d verdict fixtures at crowns and\ncorners.\n\nThe flank now reads within one ball diameter (`ridge::reach`) and asks\nthe cusp's own geometry (`stock_sim::ridge_scan::flank`):\n- only the nearest feet count (within max(cell, 3·tol) of the nearest\n  distance): a cusp's column stands equally far from both passes;\n- one foot per pass, at its nearest point: runs of joined segments,\n  merged by closed ring, so a pass curving round a crown or an edge is\n  one side, not a fan of chord feet; a free end gives no side;\n- each side's ball must touch the part (`Access::touches`): an air or\n  skim pass has no contact path to leave a cusp beside.\n\nThe M13.8 per-chord `Flank` is retired; `scan.rs` hands the ridge pass\nto the new `ridge_scan` module (scan.rs 431 -> 358 lines).\n\nReadings: every finish3d release-lane fixture stays green (88/88) and\nevery scallop-asserted one reads 0 before and after; a flat raster now\nreads its floor point for s = 3.0 .. 5.9 (s = 4: 0.606; before: 0).\nThe morphed spiral's apex reading drops 0.132 -> 0 (one pass round the\ncrown). `verify::envelope_verdict_follows_the_stated_tol` now expects the\ntol-0.1 cone rings' real cusp (0.085) as the one non-blocking Scallop\nnote at a 0.01 budget, no envelope verdict as before.\n\nThe verifier only judges: no toolpath or posted output changes.\n\nFixes #212\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
